    },
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Prophet’s Anguish and Hope"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am the man who has seen affliction by the rod of His wrath."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has led me and made me walk",
          "In darkness and not in light."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Surely He has turned His hand against me",
          "Time and time again throughout the day."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has aged my flesh and my skin,",
          "And broken my bones."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has besieged me",
          "And surrounded me with bitterness and woe."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has set me in dark places",
          "Like the dead of long ago."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has hedged me in so that I cannot get out;",
          "He has made my chain heavy."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Even when I cry and shout,",
          "He shuts out my prayer."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has blocked my ways with hewn stone;",
          "He has made my paths crooked."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has been to me a bear lying in wait,",
          "Like a lion in ambush."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has turned aside my ways and torn me in pieces;",
          "He has made me desolate."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has bent His bow",
          "And set me up as a target for the arrow."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has caused the arrows of His quiver",
          "To pierce my loins."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have become the ridicule of all my people—",
          "Their taunting song all the day."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has filled me with bitterness,",
          "He has made me drink wormwood."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has also broken my teeth with gravel,",
          "And covered me with ashes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have moved my soul far from peace;",
          "I have forgotten prosperity."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "And I said, “My strength and my hope",
          "Have perished from the Lord.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Remember my affliction and roaming,",
          "The wormwood and the gall."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My soul still remembers",
          "And sinks within me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "This I recall to my mind,",
          "Therefore I have hope."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Through the Lord’s mercies we are not consumed,",
          "Because His compassions fail not."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They are new every morning;",
          "Great is Your faithfulness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“The Lord is my portion,” says my soul,",
          "“Therefore I hope in Him!”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord is good to those who wait for Him,",
          "To the soul who seeks Him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It is good that one should hope and wait quietly",
          "For the salvation of the Lord."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It is good for a man to bear",
          "The yoke in his youth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him sit alone and keep silent,",
          "Because God has laid it on him;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him put his mouth in the dust—",
          "There may yet be hope."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him give his cheek to the one who strikes him,",
          "And be full of reproach."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the Lord will not cast off forever."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Though He causes grief,",
          "Yet He will show compassion",
          "According to the multitude of His mercies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For He does not afflict willingly,",
          "Nor grieve the children of men."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "To crush under one’s feet",
          "All the prisoners of the earth,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "To turn aside the justice due a man",
          "Before the face of the Most High,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          36
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Or subvert a man in his cause—",
          "The Lord does not approve."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          37
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is he who speaks and it comes to pass,",
          "When the Lord has not commanded it?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          38
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Is it not from the mouth of the Most High",
          "That woe and well-being proceed?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          39
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why should a living man complain,",
          "A man for the punishment of his sins?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          40
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let us search out and examine our ways,",
          "And turn back to the Lord;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          41
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let us lift our hearts and hands",
          "To God in heaven."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          42
        ],
        "lines": [
          "We have transgressed and rebelled;",
          "You have not pardoned."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          43
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have covered Yourself with anger",
          "And pursued us;",
          "You have slain and not pitied."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          44
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have covered Yourself with a cloud,",
          "That prayer should not pass through."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          45
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have made us an offscouring and refuse",
          "In the midst of the peoples."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          46
        ],
        "lines": [
          "All our enemies",
          "Have opened their mouths against us."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          47
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Fear and a snare have come upon us,",
          "Desolation and destruction."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          48
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My eyes overflow with rivers of water",
          "For the destruction of the daughter of my people."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          49
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My eyes flow and do not cease,",
          "Without interruption,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          50
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Till the Lord from heaven",
          "Looks down and sees."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          51
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My eyes bring suffering to my soul",
          "Because of all the daughters of my city."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          52
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My enemies without cause",
          "Hunted me down like a bird."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          53
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They silenced my life in the pit",
          "And threw stones at me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          54
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The waters flowed over my head;",
          "I said, “I am cut off!”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          55
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I called on Your name, O Lord,",
          "From the lowest pit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          56
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have heard my voice:",
          "“Do not hide Your ear",
          "From my sighing, from my cry for help.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          57
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You drew near on the day I called on You,",
          "And said, “Do not fear!”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          58
        ],
        "lines": [
          "O Lord, You have pleaded the case for my soul;",
          "You have redeemed my life."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          59
        ],
        "lines": [
          "O Lord, You have seen how I am wronged;",
          "Judge my case."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          60
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have seen all their vengeance,",
          "All their schemes against me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          61
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have heard their reproach, O Lord,",
          "All their schemes against me,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          62
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The lips of my enemies",
          "And their whispering against me all the day."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          63
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Look at their sitting down and their rising up;",
          "I am their taunting song."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          64
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Repay them, O Lord,",
          "According to the work of their hands."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          65
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Give them a veiled heart;",
          "Your curse be upon them!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          66
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In Your anger,",
          "Pursue and destroy them",
          "From under the heavens of the Lord."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
